  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps the 55 °C test and buyer access to complete per-model results but raises the permanent ceiling to 6.5% (with a 12-month remediation window above 5%), which is the main weakening and protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while S4's 36-month suppression deadline is the Halcyon-favoured term. S1 requires 24-hour reporting for all thermal incidents, which affects both companies' unreported incidents."
